   "title": "Ask Ethan: What does it mean for atoms to “touch” each other?",
   "snippet": "One of the most counterintuitive things about existence is the notion of forces. In order to experience a force — that is, for one object to feel the influence of another object on it — two objects don’t necessarily even need to touch, or be in contact, with one another. Objects on Earth’s surface feel Earth’s gravity, but so do airplanes, satellites, and even the Moon: in the atmosphere, in low-E",
